                      (    forth6809.asm):03866                                   ; memory on return. Since UNLOOP has no
                      (    forth6809.asm):03867                                   ; other legitimate use than immediately
                      (    forth6809.asm):03868                                   ; preceding an exit from the definition, and
                      (    forth6809.asm):03869                                   ; EXIT already handles that correctly on its
                      (    forth6809.asm):03870                                   ; own, UNLOOP is now a true no-op rather than
